session Pure_Pattern in Pure_Pattern = HOL +
  description \<open>
    A faithful formalization of Isabelle/Pure's pattern unification and matching
    (src/Pure/pattern.ML, including sorts, Type.unify and Envir), with a fix of the
    occurs check, from which a drop-in replacement for pattern.ML is generated.
  \<close>
  sessions
    "HOL-Library"
  theories
    Pure_Pattern_Code
    Pure_Pattern_Test

session Pure_Unify in Pure_Unify = Pure_Pattern +
  description \<open>
    A faithful formalization of Isabelle/Pure's higher-order unification
    (src/Pure/unify.ML), from which a drop-in replacement for unify.ML is generated.
  \<close>
  theories
    Pure_Unify_Code
    Pure_Unify_Test

session Pure_Thm in Pure_Thm = Pure_Pattern +
  description \<open>
    A faithful formalization of the inference rules of Isabelle/Pure (src/Pure/thm.ML): the
    primitive rules, the derived rules (generalization, instantiation, lifting, proof by
    assumption, flex-flex pairs, permutation of premises, type variables) and the composition
    of theorems (bicompose_aux, the inference behind resolution), with their classic and tight
    proofs, from which a replacement of these rules in thm.ML is generated.
  \<close>
  sessions
    Pure_Unify
  theories
    Pure_Bicompose_Code

session Pure_Thm_Test in Pure_Thm_Test = Pure_Thm +
  description \<open>
    Differential tests of the code generated in session Pure_Thm against the inference rules of
    Isabelle/Pure (structures Thm, Proofterm and ZTerm), on problems taken from the theorems of
    HOL.
  \<close>
  theories
    Pure_Bicompose_Test
    Pure_Proofterm_Test
    Pure_Assumption_Test
    Pure_Rules_Test

session Thm_Correctness in Thm_Correctness = HOL +
  description \<open>
    Soundness of the formalization of the composition of theorems of Isabelle/Pure
    (bicompose_aux, session Pure_Thm) on the lambda-calculus of session Pure_Lambda, with the
    results on higher-order unification of session Unify_Correctness. A theorem is valid in a
    model of the meta-logic if each of its instances holds whose flex-flex pairs are solved and
    whose hypotheses hold; an instance is given by a certified, well-sorted type instantiation
    and a substitution of the schematic variables by closed well-typed terms without schematic
    variables (type variables are allowed). The classic and tight proofs that biresolution
    attaches to its results are valid proofs of them (theory Thm_Type: one abstract type of
    theorems with both proofs).
  \<close>
  sessions
    Pure_Lambda
    Pure_Pattern
    Pure_Unify
    Pure_Thm
    Pattern_Correctness
    Unify_Correctness
  theories
    Thm_Syntax
    Thm_Model
    Thm_Semantics
